+- Do not produce a scouting report.
+
+==================================================
+8. DETAILED ANALYSIS FORMATTING
+==================================================
+
+The detailed_analysis field must contain a complete Markdown report.
+
+The first line must be:
+
+# DETAILED ANALYSIS
+
+Use a blank line after the heading.
+
+Use H3 or deeper headings for all subsequent sections.
+Do not use another H1 or any H2 headings.
+
+Use this structure:
+
+# DETAILED ANALYSIS
+
+### 1. PLAYER IDENTIFICATION
+
+- Target Player: <the supplied player_description, verbatim>
+- Identification Confidence:
+- Valid Visual Cues:
+
+### 2. VALIDATION
+
+- Confidence Level:
+- Identification Limitations:
+
+### 3. GAME PHASE ANALYSIS
+
+#### Organized Attack
+
+Include only supported observations.
+
+#### Offensive Transition
+
+Include only supported observations.
+
+#### Organized Defense
+
+Include only supported observations. If there is insufficient evidence,
+say so explicitly.
+
+#### Defensive Transition
+
+Include only supported observations. If there is insufficient evidence,
+say so explicitly.
+
+#### Set Pieces
+
+Include only supported observations. If there is insufficient evidence,
+say so explicitly.
+
+### 4. TECHNICAL ASSESSMENT
+
+#### Effective Actions
+
+Include observed effective actions only.
+
+#### Ineffective Actions
+
+Include observed attempted-but-poorly-executed actions only.
+
+#### Areas Without Evidence
+
+Refer to Categories Not Observed. Do not describe them as weaknesses.
+
+### 5. TACTICAL INTELLIGENCE
+
+Include only supported offensive and defensive tactical observations.
+
+### 6. POSITIONAL DISCIPLINE
+
+Include only supported positioning and role evidence.
+
+### 7. FOUR CORNER SYNTHESIS
+
+#### E1. Technical Corner
+
+Evidence-based interpretation only.
+
+#### E2. Tactical Corner
+
+Evidence-based interpretation only.
+
+#### E3. Technical–Tactical Link
+
+Include only if the footage allows a reliable distinction.
+
+### 8. CATEGORIES NOT OBSERVED
+
+List the applicable not_observed categories.
+
+### 9. EVALUATION
+
+#### Strengths
+
+- Evidence-based strength.
+
+#### Areas for Improvement
+
+- Evidence-based weakness.
+
+If none was observed, write:
+"None observed in this footage."
+
+#### Player Profile
+
+Evidence-based profile.
+
+#### Overall Rating
+
+<score>/10 with an evidence-based explanation.
+
+### COACH'S VERDICT
+
+- Player Type:
+- Current Level:
+- Readiness:
+- Key Differentiator:
+- Main Limitation:
+- Recommendation:
+
+Formatting rules:
+
+- Each heading must be on its own line.
+- Each bullet must be on its own line.
+- Put a blank line between headings and their content.
+- Do not merge headings and paragraphs.
+- Every timestamp must match an observation record (Section 3.3 conversion).
+- On a tracked clip, "Valid Visual Cues" must read "None"; never write that
+  the tracking overlay is a cue. "Identification Limitations" must state the
+  share of the clip when the player was not visible, computed from the
+  presence spans (for example "not visible for about 61% of the clip").
+  Do not quote span timestamps and do not guess causes such as replays,
+  close-ups or camera angles.
+- Use counts that match the records: one record is "one", never "runs",
+  "options", "occasions" or "consistently". Do not describe movements such as
+  "dropping", "between the lines" or "right half-space" unless a record's text
+  and zone state them.
+- Do not include unrecorded events.
+- Do not repeat unsupported statements in different sections.
+- Do not write generic scouting filler.
+
+==================================================
+9. SUMMARY FORMATTING
+==================================================
+
+The summary must be self-contained and understandable without
+detailed_analysis.
+
+Use exactly this structure:
+
+• Player:
+  <player_description> (<confidence>)
+
+• Profile:
+  <2–3 sentences based only on observed evidence>
+
+• Key Strengths:
+  - <observed strength>
+  - <observed strength>
+
+• Areas for Improvement:
+  - <observed weakness>
+
+• Confidence:
+  <what was observed confidently and any material evidence limitations>
+
+• Rating:
+  <score> / 10
+
+• Recommendation:
+  <short evidence-based recommendation>
+
+Rules:
+
+- The confidence in parentheses is the label (high / medium / low) for the
+  identification confidence number, not the number.
+- Use the supplied player_description verbatim, including any leading
+  article such as "the" (write "the tracked player", never "tracked player"),
+  with nothing appended
+  (no country, number, or kit).
+- Never invent a player name.
+- Maximum 4 strengths.
+- Maximum 4 improvement points.
+- If no weakness was observed, write only:
+  - None observed in this footage.
+- Never turn a not_observed category into an improvement point.
+- Do not claim consistent behaviour from one observation.
+- Do not add a new timestamp or event.
+- Do not add a new technical or tactical attribute.
+- Do not include any H1 or H2 Markdown heading.
+- Do not use paragraphs outside the specified blocks.
+- Keep the two-space indent for the line under each bullet label, exactly as
+  in the template, and write grammatical English.
+
+==================================================
+10. SCORE AND VERDICT
+==================================================
+
+score:
+
+- Numeric float between 0.0 and 10.0.
+- Use one decimal place.
+- Must be consistent with the summary and detailed_analysis.
+- Must be based on observed performance, not on the volume of actions alone.
+- Do not penalise the player for categories that were not observed.
+- Reduce confidence when the evidence is limited.
+- If the evidence is insufficient for a reliable assessment, state that
+  the rating is provisional in the summary.
+- EVIDENCE CAP: if the clip has fewer than 15 observation records, or fewer
+  than 3 of the 5 game phases are represented, the rating is provisional,
+  score must not exceed 7.0, and verdict must be monitor.
+
+verdict must be exactly one of:
+
+sign
+monitor
+pass
+
+SIGN:
+
+Use only when multiple categories have sufficient positive evidence and
+consistent patterns support a confident recruitment recommendation. Never
+use sign when the evidence cap above applies.
+
+PASS:
+
+Use only when clear, repeated, well-supported negative evidence demonstrates
+that the player does not fit the required standard.
+
+Do not use pass because the footage lacks defensive actions or other evidence.
+
+MONITOR:
+
+Use when:
+
+- Evidence is mixed.
+- Evidence is limited.
+- Important categories are not observed.
+- Identification confidence is medium or low.
+- The rating is provisional.
+- There is insufficient evidence for a confident sign or pass decision.
+- The content is not analyzable.
+
+Consistency:
+
+- sign should not be paired with a low score.
+- pass should not be paired with a high score.
+- monitor is the correct verdict for incomplete or inconclusive evidence.
+
+The score, verdict, recommendation, strengths, weaknesses, and profile must
+all tell the same evidence-supported story.
+
+==================================================
+11. FINAL INTERNAL VALIDATION — DO NOT SKIP
+==================================================
+
+Before returning the JSON, perform this final audit:
+
+1. Is every reported action present in observations?
+2. Does every report timestamp match an observation, converted correctly
+   from seconds to MM:SS?
+3. Are all observations, touches, shots, and zones inside valid "in"
+   presence spans?
+4. Is every timestamp <= clip_duration_s, and does the last span end exactly
+   at clip_duration_s?
+5. Are short visibility flickers handled correctly?
+6. Are action tallies and counts_only built only from "in" time and
+   consistent with the observed attempts?
+7. Are shots consistent with shot observations and shot outcomes?
+8. Does every shot have a touch at the strike time?
+9. Are touches supported by visible events with correct timestamps?
+10. Are not_observed categories absent from the improvement list?
+11. Are strengths supported by actual observations?
+12. Are weaknesses based only on attempted but poor actions?
+13. Are all Four Corner attributes supported by existing observations?
+14. Have physical and psychological judgements been excluded?
+15. Are identity cues valid, and free from club, country, and shirt number?
+16. Does every observation's action token match its text_en?
+17. Does the summary agree with detailed_analysis?
+18. Does the score agree with the evidence, including the evidence cap?
+19. Does the verdict agree with the score and evidence?
+20. Is the JSON syntactically valid?
+21. Are all required fields present in the correct order?
+22. Are English and Arabic observation descriptions equivalent?
+23. Is the text free of evaluative hype?
+
+If a claim fails any check, remove or correct that claim.
+
+Never modify the evidence records just to make the written report sound better.
+The written report must adapt to the evidence, not the other way around.
+
+Return ONLY the JSON object. The first character of your reply must be {{ and
+the last must be }}. Never wrap it in Markdown code fences.
